<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμέω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμός</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be squalid</i> or
				<i>unwashed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμεῖς τε κακῶς καὶ ἀεικέα ἕσσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.250
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				442
			</span></i>; <i>to be parched,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				606d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμεῖ [φυτά</span>] <i>dry
				up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.10.7
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμάω</span></b> , part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμῶσαι</span> interpol. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμώσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					360b11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμῶντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					8.10.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμῶντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.187d
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμῶσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Apol.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμώοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					26.108
				</span></i>
			, etc.—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμέω</span> is
			always used exc. in part. acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.10B.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμᾷς</span> is cited from
				<i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				76
			</span></i> by <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.34
			</span></i>; other forms are ambiguous, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					84
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				34.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				26.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμήσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					251d
				</span></i>
			. etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
